  "body": "Follow-up to #75. Requested: *\"make sure you can independently configure opencode go and opencode zen — both add and remove the keys or set rotation type, and when done for one to happen to the other and sync\"*.\n\n4.53.0 got half of that. Both cards could add and remove keys, but the **rotation select stayed only on OpenCode Zen** — I withheld it on the reasoning that a second control bound to one variable was exactly what the field deduplication existed to prevent.\n\nThat reasoning was too cautious. `changedValues()` keys its payload by `data-key` and `updateDirtyState()` counts *keys*, not controls:\n\n```js\nvalues[input.dataset.key] = value;      // last-wins, one entry per variable\nconst count = Object.keys(changedValues()).length;\n```\n\nSo duplicate controls are only a problem if they are allowed to **disagree**. `syncSharedControls()` mirrors the value across every control bound to the same key on edit, which makes the duplicate a second *view* of one value rather than a second copy of it. Element ids stay unique via a card-scoped suffix.\n\nBoth cards now carry the whole pool: add, remove, per-key health, and rotation.\n\n## Verified in a browser\n\nNone of this is reachable from the API, so it was driven against a running server.\n\n**Both selects exist, no duplicate ids:**\n\n```json\n{\"zen\": {\"id\": \"field-OPENCODE_API_KEY_ROTATION\",                \"value\": \"single\"},\n \"go\":  {\"id\": \"field-OPENCODE_API_KEY_ROTATION--opencode_go\",   \"value\": \"single\"},\n \"duplicateIds\": []}\n```\n\n**Sync runs both directions, and stays one change:**\n\n| Edited on | Zen shows | Go shows | `changedValues()` |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Go card → `round_robin` | `round_robin` | `round_robin` | 1 key |\n| Zen card → `least_used` | `least_used` | `least_used` | 1 key |\n\n**Apply from the Go card persists**, and survives the restart that rotation requires:\n\n```\n~/.fcc/.env   OPENCODE_API_KEY_ROTATION=failover\nafter reload  zenRotation \"failover\"   goRotation \"failover\"\n              zenFace \"2 keys · Failover\"   goFace \"2 keys · Failover\"\n```\n\n**Keys sync in both directions.** Added a second key from the **Go** card, removed one from the **Zen** card:\n\n```\nafter add from Go      pool 2  [\"sk-ope…3456\", \"sk-sec…9999\"]  both faces \"2 keys · Failover\"\nafter remove from Zen  pool 1  [\"sk-ope…3456\"]                  both faces \"1 key\"\n```\n\nSuite: **6 failures on this branch, 6 on unmodified `fork/main` in the same shell, zero new** — the known PowerShell installer tests. `ruff format`, `ruff check`, `ty` and the suppression grep all pass.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- The sync is client-side JavaScript and there is no JS test harness in the repo, so it is guarded by browser verification rather than by CI. The data side — which provider owns a credential and who shares it — is covered by contract tests from #75.\n- Unrelated and pre-existing, noticed while measuring the dirty count: `BRAVE_EXTRA_SNIPPETS` reads as changed on every page load (stored `\"\"` against a checkbox reading `\"false\"`), so the Apply button is lit before you touch anything. Not touched here.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
