    "message": "fix(admin): rotation editable from either card of a shared credential\n\n4.53.0 gave OpenCode Go its own key manager but deliberately withheld the\nrotation select, on the grounds that a second control bound to one variable\nwas the thing the field deduplication existed to prevent. That left the two\ncards asymmetric: keys could be added from either, the policy only from\nOpenCode Zen.\n\nThe asymmetry was unnecessary. changedValues() keys its payload by data-key\nand updateDirtyState() counts keys rather than controls, so duplicate\ncontrols on one variable are only a problem if they are allowed to disagree.\nsyncSharedControls mirrors the value across every control bound to the same\nkey on edit, which makes the duplicate a second view of one value instead of\na second copy of it. Element ids stay unique through a card-scoped suffix.\n\nBoth cards now carry the full pool: add, remove, per-key health and rotation.\nA change on either applies to both, and the dirty counter still reports one\nchange rather than two.\n\nVerified in a browser against a running server, since none of this is\nreachable from the API:\n\n- Both cards render a rotation select; ids field-OPENCODE_API_KEY_ROTATION\n  and field-OPENCODE_API_KEY_ROTATION--opencode_go, zero duplicate ids.\n- Setting round_robin on the Go card moved the Zen card to round_robin;\n  setting least_used on the Zen card moved the Go card. changedValues()\n  reported exactly one key, OPENCODE_API_KEY_ROTATION.\n- Apply from the Go card wrote OPENCODE_API_KEY_ROTATION=failover to .env,\n  and after the restart both cards read \"2 keys - Failover\".\n- Adding a key from the Go card and removing one from the Zen card both moved\n  the pool and both card faces together (2 keys then 1, pool API agreeing).\n\nFull suite: 6 failures on this branch, 6 on unmodified fork/main in the same\nshell, zero new. ruff format, ruff check, ty and the suppression grep pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
